  "body": "## Summary\n- Give each durable `FileJournal` a named writer thread that serializes journal append writes and `sync_data` requests, replying with the I/O result.\n- Preserve the synchronous `WorldJournal::append` contract and ordering; update the writer's file handle after compaction rename, and retain the broken-journal guard if replacement fails.\n- Do not use `block_in_place`; open-time header writes use the same dedicated writer path.\n\n## Verification\n- `cargo check --lib` — passed.\n- `cargo test -p id --lib world_store::tests` — 34 passed.\n- `rustfmt --edition 2024 --check src/world_store.rs` — passed.\n- Benchmark not yet run; `many_worlds` performance and `journal_append_fsync` baseline remain to verify.\n\nCloses #5502\n",
